      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s a bit of an extrapolation. 😊 I just said I don\u0027t have a fix for that specific macro.\n\nI\u0027ve fixed a *huge* number of issues. See the \"CLs merged\" section in http://b/172020503 (e.g., https://crrev.com/c/3179314, https://crrev.com/c/3169965, https://crrev.com/c/3182621, https://crrev.com/c/3188639, plus 100 more...).\n\nEverything builds fine on the host for `clang`, so there\u0027s no reason not to use it.\n\nThe only thing preventing a full cutover for all boards are the nds32 boards described in http://go/cros-clang-for-ec-firmware and some boards that have very limited flash space: http://b/256193799.",
